---
mode: prompt
---
// H9a acceptance area (b) — typed query with a NAMED schema decl (QRY-22).
// The declared `Reply` schema is lowered and the model's response is validated
// against it.
//
// Bug 0010: the forced respond turn is dispatched OFF-SESSION through pi-ai
// `complete()` with the tool choice forced to the synthesised respond tool, so
// the validated JSON never streams as assistant text and is not on `pi -p`
// stdout by itself (the pre-0010 fused mechanism streamed the raw JSON as the
// turn's reply — that observation channel is dead). The final untyped query
// below is the fixture's own rendering of the AJV-validated value: it
// interpolates `r` (QRY-18 compact-JSON stringification) behind the committed
// sentinel the suite keys on, and its echo is the run's LAST assistant
// message — the one `pi -p` text mode prints. The sentinel can only appear if
// the typed binding resolved Ok (past AJV and past `?`), so a free-phase turn
// can never satisfy the suite's assertion.
schema Reply {
  status: string,
  summary: string
}
let r: Reply = @`Report on a hypothetical build. Set status to a single short word and summary to one sentence.`?
@`Reply with exactly this text and nothing else, no markdown, no code fences: ACC TYPED NAMED RESULT ${r}`?
